        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gabe Saporta, Robert Plant, Jimmy Page\n- Organizations: Led Zeppelin, Cobra Starship, Midtown\n- Places: New York City, New York, Bron-Yr-Aur, Wales, United States\n- Works: “Friends”\n- Topics: music careers, band formation, songwriting\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Plant was born on 20 August 1948 and is an English singer, songwriter, and musician best known as the lead singer and lyricist of Led Zeppelin.\n- Jimmy Page and Robert Plant wrote the song “Friends” in 1970 at Bron-Yr-Aur, a small cottage in Wales where they stayed after completing a concert tour of the United States.\n- Gabe Saporta was born on October 11, 1979 and is an Uruguayan-American musician and entrepreneur.\n- Cobra Starship was an American dance-pop band created by former Midtown bassist and lead vocalist Gabe Saporta in 2006 in New York City, New York.",
